From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:20:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 32/56] Skip the sound manager's per-beat pass when sound is
 off

With /nosound there is no audio engine, so nothing in UpdateSoundRequests
can play. Upstream's temporary [SNDDIAG] probes (d8f948b6) still run in
it every beat: a sweep of the whole CSndParams registry plus, for every
audible entity, a linear registry lookup under a mutex and two or three
VirtualQuery calls. In an unpaced agent game that was 70-80 % of the main
thread, which the sim thread then waited on.

Measured on one rule-policy game (SCMP_016, seed 5): game minutes 5-8
take 5 s instead of 10 s; the sim thread goes from 62 % to 98 % of a
core, the main thread from 99 % to 52 % (30 % minimized).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 81c590060a786cc21270bcda13aaf6b51f1ca332)
---
 src/sdk/moho/audio/CUserSoundManager.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sdk/moho/audio/CUserSoundManager.cpp b/src/sdk/moho/audio/CUserSoundManager.cpp
index bbbec322..42621b24 100644
--- a/src/sdk/moho/audio/CUserSoundManager.cpp
+++ b/src/sdk/moho/audio/CUserSoundManager.cpp
@@ -1015,6 +1015,13 @@ namespace moho
 
   void CUserSoundManager::UpdateSoundRequests(const gpg::fastvector<SAudioRequest>& requests)
   {
+    // Engine addition (agent bridge): without an audio engine (/nosound) nothing in this pass can
+    // play, but the [SNDDIAG] probes below still sweep the descriptor registry and VirtualQuery
+    // every audible entity each frame -- most of a /nosound training game's main thread. Skip it.
+    if (!SND_Enabled()) {
+      return;
+    }
+
     // TEMPORARY PROBE [SNDDIAG] (do not commit) -- sweep every live descriptor
     // once a beat so a corrupted one is reported on the beat it goes bad,
     // rather than later when whichever entity happens to own it enters the
